{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"d29473b7-cfa2-4279-8b43-b9a706bd5421","title":"Angles in a triangle add up to 180 degrees"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d29473b7-cfa2-4279-8b43-b9a706bd5421","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A triangle has three interior angles. Call them alpha, beta, and gamma. We will show why their sum is always 180 degrees.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Angles in a triangle"},{"op":"figure","id":"triangle","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4,5],"y":[-0.7,4.4],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[-3,0],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[3,0],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"c","at":[1,3],"label":"C"},{"kind":"polyline","id":"outline","points":[{"at":"a"},{"at":"b"},{"at":"c"}],"closed":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"a"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"c"},"r":0.16,"label":"α"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"b"},"from":{"at":"c"},"to":{"at":"a"},"r":0.16,"label":"β"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.16,"label":"γ"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d29473b7-cfa2-4279-8b43-b9a706bd5421","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Draw a line through C parallel to the base. The left side crosses both parallel lines, so these alternate interior angles are equal.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"parallel_add","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"left_end","at":[-3.5,3]},{"kind":"point","id":"right_end","at":[4.5,3]},{"kind":"segment","id":"parallel","from":{"at":"left_end"},"to":{"at":"right_end"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":{"at":"left_end"},"to":{"at":"a"},"r":0.22,"label":"α"}]},{"op":"text","id":"parallel_note","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Parallel lines give equal angles"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d29473b7-cfa2-4279-8b43-b9a706bd5421","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The right side also crosses the parallel lines, copying beta beside gamma. Now alpha, gamma, and beta sit together beneath one straight line.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"beta_add","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"c"},"from":{"at":"b"},"to":{"at":"right_end"},"r":0.22,"label":"β"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What is the total angle beneath the straight line through C?","expected_gist":"180 degrees, a straight angle"}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"d29473b7-cfa2-4279-8b43-b9a706bd5421","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Angles along a straight line total 180 degrees. Those are exactly the triangle's three angles, so every triangle has the same angle sum.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"straight_add","on":"triangle","marks":[{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"c"},"r":1.2,"start":180,"end":360,"stroke":"dashed","label":"180°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"angle_sum","anchor":{"el":"parallel_note","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\alpha+\\gamma+\\beta=180^\\circ"},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"angle_sum","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\boxed{\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=180^\\circ}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
